        "description": "In a speech at which he confirmed he would run to become Labour leader, Wes Streeting has said that he would \u2018one day\u2019 like the UK to rejoin the EU.\n\nGreater Manchester Mayor, who also wants to run, Andy Burnham has said similar things in the past, he\u2019d first have to win a by-election in Makerfield - an area that voted to leave.\n\nSo, are Labour going to go to war over the issue again? Does it put Burnham in a tricky position? And is it what the public wants?\n\n00:00 A reverse Andy Burnham\n03:36 Wes Streeting\u2019s EU speech\n4:50 A rejoiner PM?\n6:00 Nandy says Streeting suggestion is \u2018odd\u2019\n8:30 A PM in purgatory?\n11:00 What Makerfield thinks\n13:00 The Burnham effect\n17:10 The other parties\n21:20 Would a new leader have a mandate?\n23:00 Smack barms vs scrap barms\n26:00 Makerfield residents prepare \n27:20 What Starmer does\n\nFor the latest news download the BBC News app or visit BBC.com/news\n\nSubscribe to our channel here: https://bbc.in/bbcnews\n\n#Brexit #BBCNews",
